Z||000000||Cooter||01-11-2000||08:58 PM||||Well, my slave cylinder bit the big one today. So I took my 2 month old cylinder back to that store and was told that since it didn't have but a 90 day warrantee, they did not put the customer info into the computer and without a reciept I had no proof that it came from them. There's about $50 shot down the drain. Oh, well. Live and learn I guess.||||reg||1
Z||000001||kidzwheelz||01-11-2000||09:10 PM||||   Cooter, I just happen to work at Pep Boys part time nights after I'm done with the military, and I'm not sure, but I think our Raybestos slave cylinders have a lifetime warranty. Not plugging the store, mind you, just trying to be helpful. One thing for sure, don't throw away your receipts! Most of the big chain auto stores will not do refunds, exchanges, or honor warranties without a receipt.||||reg||1
Z||000002||DXR_DAD||01-11-2000||09:54 PM||||Cooter one thing I've learned with retail stores, when you have a problem you need to take it to the higher-ups (management) there is no such thing as "we can't do that" somebody can override the rule.<P>But I do keep ALL reciepts. I have a fiero file. All paper work on my cars are there and I mean every reciept. Just for me to remember all the stuff I've done||||reg||4
Z||000003||Cooter||01-11-2000||10:33 PM||||I usually keep all receipts, but for some reason, I can't find this ONE! But, I figured out a way to get my car fixed and not have $50 out of my pocket for too long. More details on my plot to get even later. . . Hahahahahah That is me lauging loudest and last!||||reg||1
Z||000004||Harry||01-11-2000||11:13 PM||||Cooter, stop going to show and shine stores!<BR>Thats all they are good for (cleaning supplies), hell they dont even sell good wire and plugs anymore.<BR>Might be close and cheap but so's there parts half the time!||||reg||12
Z||000005||william_thorniii||01-12-2000||12:08 AM||||Oddly enough the only reason that I go to Auto Zone for is for their electronic records.  I find it much easier (although I usually keep decent records) to not have to go digging in the file with my greasy hands to find the receipt.  I only buy simple things (batteries and the like), but have had great success with their computer records.  <P>Sorry to hear that you have had a bad experience though.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000006||SN1PERVII||01-12-2000||12:44 AM||||    Hi all. I work at Auto Zone and i know that if they did not put your waranty in the computer the register would have given the cashier an error mesage. The only way to sell a waranty part without a waranty in the computer is to have a manager override the program. <P>The only thing that i can think of is that they messed up putting your phone number in for the waranty. that is how all the warantys are sorted. I am trully sorry (not just because i work for them but because I Hate seeing sombody getting gyped.) <P>Did the guy helping you try searching by name too or just the phone #?  <P>Well good luck    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR><p>[This message has been edited by SN1PERVII (edited 01-12-2000).]||||reg||9
Z||000007||mrfiero||01-12-2000||01:00 AM||||Cooter,<P>You should "bite the bullet" and spend the extra $$ on a factory GM slave.  The aftermarkets slaves don't appear to be well built.  BTW....the slaves sold by Pep Boys are identical to those sold by AutoZone (just different prices).  This is true for the Getrag 5-sp. slaves.....same slaves sold under different brands.  All are a cast iron unit with too many problems to list.  The major problem I had with them was a very loose fitting bleeder screw which allowed air to enter the system.  Also the "perch" where the bleeder screws into has a tendency to snap off.....a very poor design, IMHO.<P>I bought my Formula in May '99 and replaced the badly slipping clutch a month later.  At that time I replaced the master and slave cylinders (bought them both from NAPA....you guessed it, same slave as AZ and Pep Boys).  Within a month the seal went south.  I got another one under warranty and the bleeder thing snapped off while trying to bleed it.  The next one lasted a few months before it snapped on me while bleeding it.  I have been through 4 slaves in less than a year!  I just ordered a factory GM slave and hopefully my problems will be solved.<P>That's my opinion, but I really think the quality of the aftermarket slaves is severely<BR>lacking.||||reg||1
Z||000008||fiero56||01-12-2000||10:11 AM||||I can attest to the shoddy quality of those cast iron slaves. Just  month or so ago, while bleeding my brand new slave, the "perch" for the bleeder screw cam off, making the unit useless. Took another week to a warranty replacement ordered in. The slave problem alone slowed my clutch replacement down by a week. At least Raybestos was willing to give me a new one without the receipt.||||reg||1
Z||000009||DRH||01-12-2000||11:43 AM||||Last summer I had to replace the slave on my 88 Formula because the thing the bleeder mounts in snapped off the cylinder when I tried to loosen the bleeder. From the looks of it I assumed it was the original cylinder but have no way of knowing. The funny thing is that I got one from NAPA and it is designed differently. The bleeder mounting boss does not narrow down where it meets the cylinder like the old one did. It sounds like the ones mrfiero got from NAPA are the "bad" design.||||reg||1
Z||000010||mrfiero||01-11-2000||04:34 PM||||DRH & fiero56,<P>THANKS!  You have made my day.  I thought I was the only one to have a slave "snap" in half!  Everyone that I told this story too thought I was nuts.....I'm glad (sort of) that it wasn't all my fault.  It wasn't as though I really torqued down the bleeder.....it snapped off with very little effort.<P>At any rate, I have a new GM slave on it's way and should have my Formula back on the road by the weekend.  I wish it was sooner than that, I hate putting the miles on my GT.....oh well.||||reg||7
